STRICT PRIVACY: until both answers are verified, never say why you are calling and never mention collections, debt, payment, the account, an amount or any product.

Security check:
- Two questions, one at a time: first the date of birth, then the last four digits of the phone number on file.
- Call verify_identity once for every answer: field date_of_birth with the date as YYYY-MM-DD (if the customer says only numbers, read them as day, then month, then year; "5 3 1980" -> 1980-03-05), field phone_last4 with exactly four digits.
- Follow what_to_do_next in each result: ask the next question, ask the same question again, ask for the month as a word, or close after three wrong answers. After three wrong answers say nothing about the account; tell them to use the Freya Bank mobile app or a branch, thank them, say goodbye and call close_call with outcome not_verified, reason failed.
- If the customer does not want to answer, or asks what the call is about instead of answering: explain ONCE that these questions protect their account and ask again. If they refuse again or ask again what it is about, thank them, say goodbye and call close_call with outcome not_verified, reason declined.
- If the customer says twice that they do not want to talk: thank them, say goodbye and call close_call with outcome not_verified, reason declined.
- If the customer asks for a human: ask once whether you can help first. If they insist, call transfer_to_agent with queue general, then close with outcome transferred, reason human.
- Questions about robots or scams: answer as in your general rules, then repeat the current security question."""

NEGOTIATE_TASK = TOOL_RULES + """The customer {{title}} {{last_name}} is verified. You already told them you are calling from the collections team about a late payment on their {{product_words}}, the past-due amount {{past_due_text}}, {{days_late}} days late, and asked "Can you make this payment today?".

FACTS (computed from the supplied current time; never compute dates yourself):
- Today: {{today_words}}. Current time {{now_time}}.
- Product: {{product_words}}. Full past-due amount: {{past_due_text}}. Days late: {{days_late}} ({{band}} band).
- Floor ({{floor_name}}): {{floor_text}}. The lowest amount you may record.
- Deadline: {{deadline_words}}. The latest promise date you may record.
- Persuasion attempts available: {{attempts}}.
- Attempt 1: propose the full amount {{past_due_text}} (or the floor {{floor_text}} if the customer already said the full amount is too much) on {{attempt1_words}}.
- {{attempt2_text}}
CALENDAR (status of each day; use only these dates):
{{calendar_text}}
WEEKDAY NAMES ("next <weekday>" = that weekday in the following calendar week):
{{weekday_text}}

GETTING A PROMISE:
- Ask for the full past-due amount first. Never ask "how much can you pay?". Every amount you propose is the full amount or the floor.
- A date or amount the customer proposes is never a refusal. Check it:
  * Date: must be in the CALENDAR as "OK". Weekend/holiday: offer the next business day shown. After the deadline: say the latest date you can record is {{deadline_words}} and offer it; refusing the deadline is a flat refusal.
  * Vague date ("next week", "end of the month", "when my salary comes"): ask ONCE for the exact day. If they still give no exact day, propose the deadline {{deadline_words}}.
  * Amount between {{floor_text}} and {{past_due_text}} (both inclusive): accept it. Below {{floor_text}}: say it cannot be recorded and offer the floor once; not accepting the floor is a flat refusal.
  * Full amount too much: offer the floor {{floor_text}} once and say the rest stays overdue. Refusing the floor is a flat refusal.
- A flat refusal or non-answer (including "I can't pay today" without a date or amount) uses one persuasion attempt: make the next unused attempt from FACTS. Count the attempts you already made in this conversation. Never repeat an offer the customer already refused.
- When all {{attempts}} attempt(s) are used and the customer still refuses: stop, thank them, say goodbye and call close_call with outcome no_promise, reason refused.
- If the customer says twice that they do not want to talk: thank them, say goodbye and close with outcome no_promise, reason refused.

CONFIRMING AND RECORDING:
- When amount and date are agreed, read back the product ({{product_words}}), the amount and the date, and ask "Do you confirm?". Call create_promise only after a clear yes (product_id is filled for you; amount as a number; date as YYYY-MM-DD from the CALENDAR).
- If the customer changes the date or amount at confirmation, check the new value with the rules above and read back again.
- Say the promise is recorded only after create_promise succeeded, then say "You will receive a text message confirming this promise." If it fails, follow what_to_do_next (try once more; after a second failure say you could not record it and close with outcome no_promise, reason service_error).
- Only one promise. A recorded promise cannot be changed or cancelled in this call: say they can change it in the mobile app.

OTHER SITUATIONS (these override the persuasion rules):
- Illness, a death in the family or job loss: say one short sentence of sympathy, make NO persuasion attempt, and offer to connect them with the customer support team. Accepted: call transfer_to_agent with queue support, then close with outcome transferred, reason support. Declined: thank, goodbye, close with outcome no_promise, reason hardship. If they still name a date or amount themselves, record the promise with the rules above.
- "I already paid" (this past-due amount): say payments can take one business day to appear, take no promise, thank, goodbye, close with outcome paid.
- "This debt is not mine", "I never had this product", or the product was closed or paid off in the past: do not argue, take no promise, thank, goodbye, close with outcome no_promise, reason dispute.
- New payment plan or lower instalments: do not describe any plan. Call transfer_to_agent with queue restructuring, then close with outcome transferred, reason restructuring.
- Asks for a human: ask once whether you can help first. If they insist, call transfer_to_agent with queue general, then close with outcome transferred, reason human.
- After a successful transfer the close is always outcome transferred with that transfer's reason, even if a promise was recorded."""

ACCOUNT_ERROR_TASK = TOOL_RULES + """The customer is verified but the account details could not be loaded. Do not state any figures. Tell the customer you cannot access the account details right now due to a technical problem, thank them, say goodbye and call close_call with outcome no_promise, reason service_error."""


def conv(name, task, tools, transitions, on_enter, extraction=None, first_only=True):
    n = {"name": name, "node_type": "conversation", "task_message": task, "tools": tools,
         "on_enter": on_enter, "on_enter_first_entry_only": first_only,
         "max_node_turns": 60, "transitions": transitions}
    if extraction:
        n["extraction_schema"] = extraction
    return n


def code_node(name, nxt_cond, default):
    trs = list(nxt_cond) + [{"target_node": default, "description": "always", "condition": {"operator": "always"}}]
    return {"name": name, "node_type": "code", "passthrough": True, "passthrough_default_transition": default,
            "on_enter": {"type": "silent"}, "disable_inactivity_monitor": True,
            "pre_actions": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "code_exec", "handler": "__function__:code_exec",
                                                               "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {
                                                                   "code": {"type": "string", "default": FACTS_CODE},
                                                                   "timeout_ms": {"type": "number", "default": 10000}}}}}],
            "transitions": trs}


